From 6f599a3df58d9213fc06dc3581f00f861e9633e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:48:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ds5: Route Sony effects by the active HID controller

Content correlation cannot identify the active controller when a game opens both its speaker and actuator streams on the same wrong physical endpoint. Spider-Man does this with two identical Sony controllers, so both streams remain on player two even when player one generated the action.

Publish meaningful Sony HID button, trigger, D-pad, or stick activity through transient wineserver state. Ignore packet counters and sensor noise, clear only the matching physical device on removal, and clear all state when Winebus starts or unloads. Nothing is written to the registry or prefix.

When a registered four-channel Sony effect carries real speaker or actuator data, resolve the active HID container to its raw ALSA PipeWire target. Retarget without dropping the block which triggered the switch, retaining content correlation only as a fallback when no physical HID activity is available.
---
 dlls/winebus.sys/main.c    | 184 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c | 164 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 server/device.c            |  38 ++++++++
 server/protocol.def        |  21 +++++
 4 files changed, 398 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

